MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Dot feels like a useful next step because voice control would complement the Fire TV devices I already use at home.",
    "The smart plug gives me a concrete reason to try Alexa: controlling a lamp alongside the Echo Dot. The Echo Show also interests me, although I would start with the simpler speaker."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV sticks repeat a function already covered by my 4K stick and Fire TV television, so being related to my purchases does not make them useful additions.",
    "Alexa in the car and wireless earbuds do not address my current home entertainment and security needs. The 16TB drive has a possible connection to my camcorder, but I have no clear need for that much storage."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to be treated as a reason to want more Fire TV devices, even when they add no capability I need.",
    "My interest in connected home devices seems to be stretched into interest in anything with Alexa, although where and how I would use it matters."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: I am more interested in adding a useful function than replacing a working streaming device or choosing two colors of the same speaker.",
    "A related accessory still needs an immediate purpose. An HDMI cable fits my setup, but I would wait until I need one, just as owning a camcorder does not establish a need for a large drive."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in connected home electronics but sometimes confuse related products with useful next additions."
}
